# Fleet & rover architecture

**Source of truth:** `lego-rover-esp32/WIRING.md`, `lego-rover-ros2/WIRING.md`, `c3-mini-bot/WIRING.md`, `c3-mini-bot/docs/SWARM.md`

## Compute split (current production)

**Brain** = NUC11 Ubuntu host `brain` at **192.168.3.172**. Docker stack in `/data/swarm/robot-fleet` (`rover-brain`, `fleet-brain`, `tracked-brain`, `microros-agent`, `fleet-ha`), **ROS 2 Jazzy**. dockerhost is no longer the brain.

| Bot | Fleet ID | Brain container | ESP role | ROS namespace |
|-----|----------|-----------------|----------|---------------|
| **Rover** (LEGO, dual-board) | 0 | `rover-brain` | Thin clients — drive board + ToF board | `/rover/…`, `/imu/data`, `/cmd_vel` |
| **Roby** (c3-mini) | 1 | `fleet-brain` | Thin client — servos, sonar pan, IMU, IR | `/bot1/…` |
| **Tracker** | 2 | `tracked-brain` | Thin client — tracked drive | `/bot2/…` |
| **Beaper** | 4 | — | WIP | — |

- **One micro-ROS agent** on the brain (UDP **8888**), multiplexes all ESP clients.
- **One `cmd_vel` publisher per bot** at a time.
- **allow_drive** gate via MQTT `lab/robots/allow_drive/set` (`ON`/`OFF`) → `/fleet/allow_drive`.
- micro-ROS session tolerance: agent is declared lost only after **6 consecutive missed pings** (200 ms period).

## Rover — dual-board

### Drive board: T-Display-S3 (`rover-esp`, 192.168.3.71)

| Bus / pin | Device / role |
|-----------|---------------|
| GPIO 1,2,3,10 | Motors L/R via TC78H660 (A=left, B=right) |
| GPIO 11,12 | Wheel ticks, direct GPIO ISR (95 mm wheels, 60 slits/rev, 130 mm track) |
| I2C 43/44 | MPU6050 IMU **0x68** only |
| GPIO 17/18 | Speaker / WS2812 LED ring (distance colours from the Pro S3 ToF topics) |
| GPIO 0 | Go button / E-stop |

No IR/MCP expander, no sonar, no local ToF. Env `s3_tdisplay_microros_rover_drive` (`ROVER_DRIVE_ONLY=1`). Diagnostics on `/rover/drive_diag` (1 Hz string).

### ToF board: UM Pro S3 (`rover-tof`)

- **VL53L8CX** front on its own I2C bus at **400 kHz**; **VL53L0X** left/right + **PCA9685** on the second bus.
- Publishes `/rover/tof/front`, `front_left`, `front_right`, `l8_cols`, `left`, `right`.
- Onboard ceramic antenna (`ROVER_PROS3_ANT_EXTERNAL=0`). Env `um_pros3_tof_microros`.

Transport (both boards): **WiFi micro-ROS** → brain agent `192.168.3.172:8888`.

## ESP safety priority (drive board)

Highest wins — motors are ESP's last word:

1. E-stop / low battery
2. IMU + wheel-tick stall lockout (~2.5 s)
3. Heading hold trim
4. Brain `/cmd_vel`
5. Cmd timeout (400 ms → stop)

**ESP:** sensing, publish, local safety only.  
**Brain:** explore, escape, logging — not an FSM on the ESP.

## Explore (brain)

- Reactive **picture** from L8 columns + side ToF (`ROVER_PICTURE=1`) with **steer-around** (`ROVER_PICTURE_STEER_AROUND`): slow and curve toward the open side; reverse only when boxed in, or on bump/stall.
- **Speed cap 25% usable** (`ROVER_AUTO_MAX_LINEAR=0.25`). The cmd value is the fraction of the usable motor range above the firmware's PWM floor; always quote speeds as usable %.

## c3-mini-bot (C3 Zero)

- **Direct GPIO servos** (wheels GPIO 0/1, pan GPIO 3) — no PCA9685.
- MPU6050 on I2C 8/9; sonar GPIO 5/6; TSOP on GPIO 7; beacon TX GPIO 20.
- `BOT_NAMESPACE` per bot in `platformio_private.ini`.

## Swarm coordination

- Bot-to-bot via ROS topics on the brain, not ESP mesh.

## Flashing

- Default **OTA** when bot is **stopped** (allow_drive OFF; see `ota-safety.mdc`).
- Drive board: build `s3_tdisplay_microros_rover_drive`, then `espota.py -i 192.168.3.71 -p 3232`.
- ToF board: `um_pros3_tof_microros` (USB) / `um_pros3_tof_microros_ota`.
- Mini: `c3-bot1.local` — `c3_mini_wifi_ota`

## Planned

- Camera-based mapping: FireBeetle 2 ESP32-S3 + OV3660 → RTAB-Map, Nav2, explore_lite (next milestone).

## Robot personality

Features belong **in the robot** (firmware + always-on brain), triggered by **Go button**, sensors, or timers — not manual shell scripts. See `robot-personality.mdc`.
